{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Managing the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Difficult Customers "}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le05ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " First Conditional: If and When to Talk about Real Life Situations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The Zero Conditional is used to talk about what you usually do in real-life situations. The result of the condition is always true according to the initial situation.  You use the First Conditional with if clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The Zero Conditional is also called the Present Real Conditional. It is used to talk about a situation that is always true when a general condition is met. <br/> <br/>You use the structure: <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If/when</span> \u2026 Simple Present, \u2026 Simple Present </span>or <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present \u2026  <span class=\"strong\">if/when</span> \u2026 Simple Present</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Both <span class=\"italic\">if</span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> are used in the Present Real Conditional. Using <span class=\"italic\">if</span> suggests that something happens less frequently. Using <span class=\"italic\">when</span> suggests that something happens regularly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not, will or will not happen. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future. <br/><br/>Structure:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple \u2026 will + verb \u2026</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you deal with an angry customer, you require a certain amount of caution.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you are successful in this business, it is because you moved beyond the emotions to discover the reason for their anger.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they aren't happy with the service, you will be considered \u201cjust like that last server.\u201d "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals to Express Criticism: Can, Could, Might, Should"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the modals <span class=\"italic\">can</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> or <span class=\"italic\">should</span> to express disapproval in the present or in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">can</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might </span> or  <span class=\"italic\">should</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Infinitive</span> to express criticism or disapproval in the present or in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You can be really annoying sometimes!<br/> Our waiters could step up a little more!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">can</span>, <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> or <span class=\"italic\">should</span> +<span class=\"italic\"> Perfect Infinitive</span> to express criticism or disapproval about a past situation. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You could have tried to solve this problem before it became too big.<br/> You really should have consulted me on this.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You shouldn't be causing a scene."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might be more polite."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could try to make these customers happy. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Customers can be rather demanding or domineering at times."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dissatisfied"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not satisfied because something is not as good as you had expected"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will encounter customers who are dissatisfied or unhappy when you meet them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you can use to describe difficult customers."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "improperly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in an inappropriate way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They may have been improperly served by you or one of your peers in the past. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "domineering  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "trying to control other people without considering their feelings or ideas"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Customers can be rather domineering at times."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "demanding "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expecting a lot of attention or expecting to have things exactly the way you want them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A demanding, indecisive customer can be frustrating as you try to serve their needs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go out of their way"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200btry very hard to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some customers seem to go out of their way to be offensive or to get attention. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "self-assured"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "calm and confident about what you are doing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Although they seem confident and self-assured outwardly, they may be insecure and defensive. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to exhibit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to clearly show a particular quality, emotion, or ability"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some behaviors they might exhibit are raising the voice or demanding to speak to a manager."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "You work for a large hotel chain. The company values your work and you have been transferred to a new location that has been having some problems. As the General Manager of the hotel, you are quite unhappy and even frustrated with what you have been noticing at this hotel."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm problems that might occur at a hotel."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a letter to one of your friends back home/ at your old job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include details about what has frustrated you and made you unhappy at your new job. (You work at a hotel, so be creative when it comes to reasons!)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to write in a letter format with appropriate greetings and closings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your letter to a classmate."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Hand in your letter to your teacher after you've made any necessary corrections."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss various problems that might be bothersome at a hotel."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a letter to a friend about my new job. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use appropriate greetings and closings."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my letter to a classmate."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about work and dealing with customers."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled using when or if."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express criticism using can, could, might, should."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think of customers who are being difficult? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How would you react if you didn't receive proper service in a restaurant? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What kind