": "You will encounter customers who are dissatisfied or unhappy when you meet them. They may have been improperly served by you or one of your peers in the past. Even if you were not personally involved in their previous experience, you will represent the restaurant. If they aren't happy with the service, you will be considered \u201cjust like that last server.\u201d Unfair as this may be, you could try to make these customers happy.<br/>\nCustomers can be rather demanding or domineering at times. Many times, domineering behavior is part of a personality style or it could be a reaction to past customer service encounters. A demanding, indecisive customer can be frustrating as you try to serve their needs.", "id": 2}, {"time": "70000", "image": "", "text": "Some customers seem to go out of their way to be offensive or to get attention. Although they seem confident and self-assured outwardly, they may be insecure and defensive. Some behaviors they might exhibit are raising the voice, demanding to speak to a manager, using profanity, being verbally abrupt (snapping back at you) even though you're trying to assist, calling you by your last name, which they see on your name tag, ignoring what you say, or otherwise going out of the way to be offensive or in control.", "id": 3}], "video_src": "engenn11le05ob02re2vid01"}}], "id": 3}, {"type": "text", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "I promise that by the time you can adequately serve six passengers at a time, you will serve in first class. If you spill a beverage on a passenger during turbulence, you will call me immediately. When you hear inappropriate comments from passengers, you will respond to them respectfully but firmly."}], "id": 4}]}]}